    <briefdescription>
<para>Indicates that data is received on a channel. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Each event should contain a K-frame of payload. The length of SDU should be specified in the first 2 bytes of the first K-frame. The sum of the payload lengths in received K-frames should be equal to the specified SDU length. Otherwise, application should disconnect the channel using <ref refid="group__sl__bt__l2cap_1ga524e3d7dbd73c5d98ea8332fb0f1fc1a" kindref="member">sl_bt_l2cap_close_channel</ref> command. The same should happen also if the SDU length exceeds the max_sdu of local channel endpoint. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
